====================================================================================================
   isotropic top-hat, B&O model: C = 0.038197186342;  3/(25 pi) = 0.038197186342;  ratio = 1.000000000000
   linear-quadrupole profile f_+ = f_- = (sin^2 th/2)/norm, B&O model: C = 0.0340369102 (finer grid 0.0340369102);  C/(3/(25 pi)) = 0.891084

====================================================================================================
(d) the exact energy delta instead of 2 pi delta(0) -> T (same model, same narrow band)
====================================================================================================
   int d^4(delta k) delta(d1 + d2 - d1' - d2') over the band^4 = sigma^3 x 2/3  (Irwin-Hall density at 0)
   Monte Carlo density of d1+d2-d1'-d2' at 0: 0.6704
   => P_total = (dP/dt) x T_eff with T_eff = 2 pi x 2/3/sigma = 4*pi/3/sigma = 4.1888/sigma
   => P_total (mean number of photon PAIRS over the whole packet history, B&O model) = 4/25 G^2 N^2 omega^3 sigma = 0.160000 G^2 N^2 omega^3 sigma;  photons = 2 x pairs.
